Patch 01 — Oscillator: compute the ARM overflow flag in C (native port)
Origin: mechanical-dance/PHX-D01, patches/01-oscillator-overflow-flag.patch
(GPL-3.0; see NOTICE). Kept byte-identical to PHX-D01's patch below this header.

Why: Oscillator.c calcNoise() reads the Cortex-M APSR overflow (V) flag via
__get_APSR() to detect the signed overflow of the phase-accumulator add. There
is no APSR on a host CPU, so the patch computes the same condition explicitly
from the operands: overflow iff the sign bits of prev and phaseInc agree and
the sign of the result differs. Muse's independent host-compile audit of the
firmware (Oct 28, 2026) flagged the identical spot before PHX-D01 was read.

--- a/Core/Src/Soundengine/DSPAudio/Oscillator.c
+++ b/Core/Src/Soundengine/DSPAudio/Oscillator.c
@@ -342,12 +342,13 @@
 //-----------------------------------------------------------
 int16_t calcNoise(OscInfo* osc)
 {
+	const uint32_t prev = osc->phase;
 	osc->phase += osc->phaseInc;
 
 	//check overflow flag, ( if osc->phase == osc->phaseInc a reset occured ==> retrigger, too
-	APSR_Type apsr;
-	apsr.w = __get_APSR();
-	if(apsr.b.V ||  (osc->phase == osc->phaseInc))
+	// native: the ARM V flag (signed overflow of the add), computed explicitly
+	const int signedOverflow = (int32_t)((prev ^ osc->phase) & (osc->phaseInc ^ osc->phase)) < 0;
+	if(signedOverflow ||  (osc->phase == osc->phaseInc))
 	{
 		//overflow happened -> phaseWrapped
 
